    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d672">

                <pb facs="0628" n="616" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg616"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/10–1944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Pinkerton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-19T16:00:00+03:00">October 19, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>153. Arab reaction to recent American statements on Palestine<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d672-f1"/> has been heretofore restricted to rather mild newspaper
                    editorials and private conversations protesting against them. There have been no
                    organized protests. Yesterday afternoon, however, Arab Chamber of Commerce
                    canceled appointment with Culbertson Mission<anchor n="20" xml:id="d672-f2"/>
                    members now visiting Palestine and said, “We would like this action of the
                    Chamber to be read as a protest against the President’s pronouncement, and as a
                    sign of our unlimited disappointment.” Mission left this morning for Haifa, Tel
                    Aviv and Jaffa where it expects to meet Jewish and Arab organizations and upon
                    its return I will report as to its reception in those cities. Mr. Culbertson
                    himself has not yet arrived in Palestine.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pinkerton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d672-f1" n="19" xml:id="d672-f1-content">
                <p>See letter from President Roosevelt to Senator Wagner, October 15, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra;</hi> for statements by Governor Thomas E. Dewey
                    and others, see footnotes 21 and 24, <ref target="#pg617">pp. 617</ref> and <ref
                        target="#pg618">618</ref>, respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d672-f2" n="20" xml:id="d672-f2-content">
                <p>For correspondence regarding the Special Economic Mission to the Middle East,
                    headed by William S. Culbertson, see <ref target="#pg38">pp. 38</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
